Subject: =?UTF-8?q?=F0=9F=94=95=20Stop=20the=20status=20upstream=20fetch?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20when=20the=20Git=20fetch=20interval=20is=200?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviour: with Settings → Source Control → Git fetch interval = 0 the server
spawns no automatic `git fetch` at all. Until now only VcsStatusBroadcaster
honoured the setting (upstream #13253 for #13235); the Git driver core's
refreshStatusUpstreamIfStale still ran `git fetch --quiet --no-tags
--no-auto-gc <remote>` from every statusDetails() call and from
statusDetailsRemote() unless the caller passed refreshUpstream: false (15 s
success TTL, failure backoff up to 15 min). GitManager.status / remoteStatus
without options, the git action flows (completion toast, PR step, worktree
reuse, stacked actions), startup auto-pull and repository publishing all
reached it, so every project on a git@github.com remote raised a 1Password SSH
prompt attributed to T3 Code, dozens a day. Non-zero intervals keep the same
cache, timeouts and backoff. Upstream PR: fix/status-fetch-honours-interval
(cherry-pick of f21bb9f6c4 on origin/main b8c2cfad6b); upstream issue #13912
is the same loop against a Keychain prompt. RETIRE this commit when the
upstream PR merges.

Port to e07585e5fb:
- GitVcsDriverCore.ts: the VcsAutomaticFetchInterval import sits next to upstream's new unsetInheritedRepositoryEnv import from VcsProcess.ts. refreshStatusUpstreamIfStale on e07585e5fb still fetches without reading the interval, so the guard is unchanged.

Files:
- apps/server: src/vcs/VcsAutomaticFetchInterval.ts (new; the Context.Reference
  and its settings-backed layer, moved out of VcsStatusBroadcaster.ts),
  src/vcs/GitVcsDriverCore.ts (captures the reference at construction;
  refreshStatusUpstreamIfStale returns before any git process when the
  interval is zero), src/vcs/VcsStatusBroadcaster.ts (imports the moved
  reference), src/server.ts (provides the layer once at the root of
  layerRuntimeDependencies so the memoised GitVcsDriver.layer captures it;
  the broadcaster-local provision removed).

Tests:
- apps/server/src/vcs/GitVcsDriverCore.test.ts: "does not fetch for status
  when the automatic fetch interval is zero" (fails on the base: one fetch).
- apps/server/src/vcs/VcsStatusBroadcaster.test.ts: import moved.

(cherry picked from commit f21bb9f6c4d56283271479e170330713e1315d2c)
